obexd: don't gate the bluetooth transport on a logind session

bluez 5.87 wraps obexd's bluetooth transport registration in logind
session tracking (obexd/src/logind.c, new since 5.79): the transport
only registers once the daemon's uid has an "active" logind session.
Upstream ships obexd as a systemd *user* unit where that holds; on a
headless appliance running obexd as a system service, root's logind
state is permanently "offline", the init callbacks never fire, and
obexd dies at startup with "obex_server_init failed: No transport
driver registered" - no AVRCP cover art.

(If logind were absent entirely, the FAIL path already falls back to
active=TRUE; only a present-but-sessionless logind wedges it.)

Treat the appliance as always active and skip the monitoring.

Upstream is unlikely to want this as-is (the right fix is probably a
configuration knob); carried locally by boompi.

--- a/obexd/src/logind.c
+++ b/obexd/src/logind.c
@@ -162,6 +162,14 @@ static int logind_init(void)
 
 	DBG("");
 
+	/* boompi: headless appliance - obexd runs as a system service
+	 * with no logind session, so session-gating would leave the
+	 * bluetooth transport permanently disabled (obex_server_init
+	 * fails at startup). Treat the box as always active. */
+	monitoring_enabled = FALSE;
+	active = TRUE;
+	return 0;
+
 	if (!monitoring_enabled)
 		return 0;
 
